{title: Majesty (FJ_169_en)}
{song_number: 169}
{language: en}
{tempo: 68}
{comment: Martin Smith und Stuart Garrard}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F#m]Here [E]I am, [Dmaj7]humbled by Your [A]majesty,
[Dmaj7]covered [A]by Your grace so [E]free.
[F#m]Here [E]I am, [Dmaj7]knowing I'm a [A]sinful man,
[Dmaj7]covered [A]by the blood of the [E]Lamb.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F#m]Here [E]I am, [Dmaj7]humbled by the [A]love that You give,
[Dmaj7]forgiven [A]so that I can for[E]give.
[F#m]Here [E]I stand, [Dmaj7]knowing that I'm [A]Your desire,
[Dmaj7]sanctified [A]by glory and [E]fire.
{end_of_verse}

[F#m]Now I've [E]found the [A]greatest love of all is
mine [A]since You laid down Your [D]life, the greatest sacrifice.

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Majesty, [E]majesty,
[D]Your grace has [A]found me just as I am: [E]empty
[F#m]handed, but I live in Your [D]hands.
[A]Majesty, [E]majesty,
[D]forever [A]I am changed by Your [E]love in the
[F#m]presence of Your majesty, [Dmaj7]majesty.
{end_of_chorus}
